    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d631-a1">

                <pb facs="0954" n="826" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg826"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 460.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Assim Pasha to Mr. Wallace</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 7,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Envoy</hi>: Referring to my note of the 30th of
                    last April, No. 74404, 19, I have the honor to inform you that after inquiry
                    made by the ministry of justice, it has been found that certain irregularities
                    occurred in the management of the affairs concerning Dr. Maurice Pflaum, an
                    American citizen. The examining magistrate, as well as the recorder of the court
                    of Asos, have, consequently, been removed, and the president of the tribunal,
                    himself, has been duly reprimanded.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ASSIM.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
